rivedAnswer":"2n+1","reason":"Starting with 3 at n=1 and adding 2 for each subsequent index gives 3+2(n-1)=2n+1.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"cn-math","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_015"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_030_q1","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p060","cnm_025","cnm_015"],"id":"count-the-increases","label":"Count the increases","methodDirectNodeIds":{"count-the-increases":["cnm_030"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_030","cnm_p060","cnm_025","cnm_015"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"alignmentIds":["alignment:f4b9ccf54864fa9fb0909af9"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"76 matchsticks","reason":"For n squares the count is 4+3(n-1)=3n+1; at n=25 this is 76.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"cn-math","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_015"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_030_q4","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p038","cnm_015","cnm_018"],"id":"count-added-matchsticks","label":"Count the added matchsticks","methodDirectNodeIds":{"count-added-matchsticks":["cnm_030"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_030","cnm_p038","cnm_015","cnm_018"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"alignmentIds":["alignment:f4b9ccf54864fa9fb0909af9"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"65535","reason":"Insert the factor 2-1=1. Successive products become 2^2-1, 2^4-1, 2^8-1, and finally 2^16-1=65535.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"cn-math","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_015"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_147_q5","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_015"],"id":"solution:successive-differences-of-squares:f766d8c05681","label":"Successive differences of squares","methodDirectNodeIds":{"successive-differences-of-squares":["cnm_147","cnm_143"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_147","cnm_143","cnm_015"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"alignmentIds":["alignment:f4b9ccf54864fa9fb0909af9"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D; -2ab cos C is negative and c²<a²+b²","reason":"Side lengths a,b are positive and an acute C has cos C>0. Thus -2ab cos C<0, and c²=a²+b²-2ab cos C<a²+b².","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"cn-math","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_015"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_h091_q4","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_015","cnm_096"],"id":"m1","label":"Sign of the cosine correction","methodDirectNodeIds":{"m1":["cnm_h061","cnm_h091"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h061","cnm_h091","cnm_015","cnm_096"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:f4b9ccf54864fa9fb0909af9"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 5s+80n","reason":"Each original value t becomes 5(t+20)-20=5t+80. Summing over n values gives 5s+80n.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_015"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1958_AMC_12_Q26","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_015","cnm_025"],"id":"track-the-total","label":"Track the sum through the operations","methodDirectNodeIds":{"track-the-total":["cnm_027","cnm_035","cnm_034"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_027","cnm_035","cnm_034","cnm_015","cnm_025"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:f4b9ccf54864fa9fb0909af9"],"answerCheck":{"adjudication":"Native reconciliation under the recorded task assumptions; no blind-review claim.","derivedAnswer":"A, 1/32","reason":"Order u<=v<=w<=2u, so w=1-u-v, 1/5<=u<=1/3 and max(u,1-3u)<=v<=(1-u)/2. For fixed u the concave quadratic u*v*(1-u-v) is increasing up to that upper endpoint, so its minimum is at the lower v bound. For u in [1/5,1/4], 32*(2u^2*(1-3u))-1=(1-4u)*(48u^2-4u-1)>=0; with t=u-1/5 the second factor is 48t^2+(76/5)t+3/25>0. For u in [1/4,1/3], 32*u^2*(1-2u)-1=(4u-1)*(-16u^2+4u+1)>=0, since the second factor is at least 2/9. Equality is attainable at permutations of (1/4,1/4,1/2). This is a complete elementary route using existing scopes.","recordedAnswer":"A","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_015"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1982_AMC_12_Q29","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_015","cnm_096"],"id":"redistribute-to-ratio-boundary","label":"Separate the smallest and largest entries","methodDirectNodeIds":{"redistribute-to-ratio-boundary":["cnm_h019","cnm_h018","cnm_146"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h019","cnm_h018","cnm_146","cnm_015","cnm_096"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:f4b9ccf54864fa9fb0909af9"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, Friday","reason":"If M_n is the millet just after the nth addition, M_1 = 1/4 and M_n = (3/4)M_(n-1)+1/4. Millet exceeds half the seeds exactly when M_n > 3/4. Thursday gives 175/256 < 3/4, while Friday gives 781/1024 > 3/4.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_015"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2009_AMC_10B_Q14","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p196","cnm_p178","cnm_p169"],"id":"reference-amount-shortfall","label":"Track the shortfall from a reference amount","methodDirectNodeIds":{"reference-amount-shortfall":["cnm_h200","cnm_015"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h200","cnm_015","cnm_p196","cnm_p178","cnm_p169"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:f4b9ccf54864fa9fb0909af9"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 9 and 5","reason":"The difference is 99(h-u). Since 1≤h-u≤9 and its units digit is 4, h-u=6. Thus the difference is 594, whose next digits from right to left are 9 and 5.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_015"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1955_AMC_12_Q37","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p053","cnm_026","cnm_015"],"id":"place-value-cancellation","label":"Method 2: Cancel the tens contribution","methodDirectNodeIds":{"place-value-cancellation":["cnm_p055","cnm_027","cnm_036"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p055","cnm_027","cnm_036","cnm_p053","cnm_026","cnm_015"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:f4b9ccf54864fa9fb0909af9"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C: 25sqrt(5)","reason":"Factoring gives 3*4^(x-1)=24, hence 2^(2x-2)=8 and x=5/2. Therefore (2x)^x=5^(5/2)=25sqrt(5).","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_015"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1958_AMC_12_Q20","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_015","cnm_042","cnm_167"],"id":"factor-and-compare-powers","label":"Factor the common power","methodDirectNodeIds":{"factor-and-compare-powers":["math:real-exponent-laws","cnm_h042","cnm_h039"]},"nodeIds":["math:real-exponent-laws","cnm_h042","cnm_h039","cnm_015","cnm_042","cnm_167"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:f4b9ccf54864fa9fb0909af9"],"answerCheck":{"adjudication":"Root independently inspected the displayed stem, choices and mathematical counterexamples or ordinary task convention.","derivedAnswer":"B for positive terms with the displayed quotient defined; no universal formula as printed","reason":"For nonzero geometric terms the reversed-pair product K gives S=K*Sprime and P^2=K^n. Positive terms select the keyed positive value. However (-1,-1,-1) gives S=Sprime=-3 and product-1, while B gives+1. Also (1,-1) has nonzero reciprocals but S=Sprime=0, so B is undefined. The printed task does not require positive terms or nonzero reciprocal sum. Preserve B with its conditions and recognize these counterexamples.","recordedAnswer":"B","status":"confirmed_ambiguous"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_015"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":["The question does not state that the terms are positive; taking the positive square-root branch can lose the sign of P.","Nonzero terms do not ensure S' is nonzero, so S/S' need not be defined.","Positivity is not stated. For odd n, the displayed fractional-power formula can lose the sign of P.","Nonzero terms do not ensure S′ ≠ 0; zero-sum progressions can make S/S′ undefined.","The unconditional identities S = CS′ and P² = C^n remain valid, but they do not establish an unconditional listed answer.","confirmed_answer_ambiguity"],"questionId":"1971_AMC_12_Q33","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_h207","cnm_016","cnm_015"],"id":"reverse-pair-products-with-sign-check","label":"Pair opposite terms and check the missing conditions","methodDirectNodeIds":{"reverse-pair-products-with-sign-check":["cnm_h208","cnm_h039","cnm_071"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h208","cnm_h039","cnm_071","cnm_h207","cnm_016","cnm_015"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:f4b9ccf54864fa9fb0909af9"],"answerCheck":{"adjudication":"Native reconciliation under the recorded task assumptions; no blind-review claim.","derivedAnswer":"D; all real x if the constant condition holds, no x otherwise","reason":"The compositions are mpx+mq+n and pmx+pn+q. Their x coefficients agree automatically. Equality is therefore equivalent to mq+n-pn-q=n(1-p)-q(1-m)=0, independently of x.","recordedAnswer":"D","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_015"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1976_AMC_12_Q10","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_196","cnm_040","cnm_015"],"id":"expand-compositions","label":"Expand the two compositions","methodDirectNodeIds":{"expand-compositions":["math:function-composition-iteration","cnm_145","cnm_034"]},"nodeIds":["math:function-composition-iteration","cnm_145","cnm_034","cnm_196","cnm_040","cnm_015"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:f4b9ccf54864fa9fb0909af9"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, 25","reason":"The factors must include both 1 and -1, since otherwise at least four have magnitude at least 3. The remaining magnitudes are 3,3,5, forcing the factor set {-3,-1,1,3,5}. Its sum is 5, so a+b+c+d+e=30-5=25.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_015"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2007_AMC_12A_Q14","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p156","cnm_015","cnm_p153","cnm_007"],"id":"force-distinct-factors","label":"Restrict the five distinct factors","methodDirectNodeIds":{"force-distinct-factors":["math:integer-diophantine-equations","math:prime-factorization"]},"nodeIds":["math:integer-diophantine-equations","math:prime-factorization","cnm_p156","cnm_015","cnm_p153","cnm_007"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:f4b9ccf54864fa9fb0909af9"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, 17/8","reason":"For the order a,b,c,d,e, the result is (a+b+2c+4d+8e)/16. Pairing larger numbers with larger weights gives the maximum 65/16, while reversing the pairing gives the minimum 31/16. Their difference is 34/16=17/8.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_015"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2012_AMC_10A_Q13","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_211","cnm_018","cnm_015"],"id":"solution:weighted-average-exchange:ec169378ae30","label":"Position weights and exchanges","methodDirectNodeIds":{"weighted-average-exchange":["math:extremal-principle","cnm_212","cnm_h019"]},"nodeIds":["math:extremal-principle","cnm_212","cnm_h019","cnm_211","cnm_018","cnm_015"]}]}],"canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_015"],"label":"乘法运算律与多个因数相乘","layer":"CN","meaning":"Practice covers aligned canonical concepts, with no claim of complete standard coverage or mastery.","nextOffset":null,"sourceNode":{"criteria":["能用分配律简算","能判断多个因数之积的符号"],"description":"把交换律、结合律、分配律推广到有理数；多个非零因数相乘时由负因数个数定符号。","id":"cnm_015","label":"乘法运算律与多个因数相乘","original":{"chapter":"七上 第二章 有理数的运算 2.2.1","description":"把交换律、结合律、分配律推广到有理数；多个非零